<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Voting under way across Brazil in tight presidential run-off between Lula and Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9192a2df1a7d19968568812c31bba71c4e6599e0e862585401cd009fdf667bc8</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:46:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonar--05fa1f528dbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s 158 million voters decide between leftist President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and right-wing challenger Senator Flavio Bolsonaro – the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro – following a highly charged run-off campaign period, with the candidates in a dead heat in polls. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Polls open in Brazil presidential runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58d2ea463d55063ef081a43445bcea160ed06906c77b83a43b744fdd63071444</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:40:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff--8d55229e95d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and sight-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro faced off Friday in their second and final debate ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff election. The two candidates repeated their campaign proposals, focusing on the cost of living and security, while exchanging ⁠allegations of corruption. France 24 Jan Onoszko telles us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Obama hits campaign trail for democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9f299f3646c8915623239cc31ea821852998cf4b50bda5c829900720bb24524</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:36:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats--dc300583e461.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">With less than two weeks to go before the US midterm elections, former President Barack Obama has hit the campaign trail, rallying support for Democratic candidates in the key states of Michigan and Ohio. He criticised the Trump administration, blaming the White House for rising living costs, a major concern for voters. Democrats are hoping to regain control of Congress, with polls showing several closely contested races. Ophelie Jacobson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know as Brazilians choose between Lula and Bolsonaro in tense presidential runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9b2ba442c14d7c494ccebeff5d2709e2ba8151c31ea75c210d3c87fc328e18</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:16:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T06:05:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff--2a6bd58b70ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilians are set on Sunday to choose between leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro in the runoff vote of a deeply polarizing presidential election, and one which will determine whether the US significantly expands its growing influence in Latin America.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US seeks to topple Cuba's government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7cdc927c1dd8b85f7f1afc172d2547bebca093231ff5c8e02437c18e83d7918</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:43:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government--b52eb58eab6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government" /><summary type="html">And now, in a rather surprising development, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is directly urging Cubans to cooperate with the CIA. Havana has responded by mocking what it calls the Trump administration’s “desperation”.</summary></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump challenges Alaska Senate trace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7648ad5ee5e79c8c6a0283dddb0c35f55b13d306dc0db6a9da2bcc6867226421</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:42:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace--8639a06bdbc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections less than two weeks away, concerns are growing over whether President Donald Trump would accept a major Republican defeat. Trump has called for legal action to block the certification of Alaska’s Senate race if Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan loses to his Democratic challenger, Mary Peltola, arguing that another candidate with the same name on the ballot could confuse voters. Our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump administration sues to block possible Democratic win in Alaska Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8d14d0bd68c5cefa3d123c95ad0ce904e7e70a929d7f1a0ab3b7216c272424a</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T11:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race--2cdc4eae1c83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that he had instructed his administration to file a lawsuit to block the certification of the US Senate race in Alaska if Republican Senator Dan Sullivan loses, arguing that voters would be confused because two Republicans on the ballot have similar names. The legal battle is ramping up questions over whether Trump will accept a potential midterms defeat.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says US may launch ‘another little Epic Fury’ attack on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b344a0ba9efebf4520c8562f4c62ae2b598d91ca98482ee83b6b04cdbc63678</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:50:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-trump-says-us-may-launch-another-little-epic-fury-attack-iran--267a801616fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-trump-says-us-may-launch-another-little-epic-fury-attack-iran" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday said his country may launch “another little Epic Fury” on Iran, referring to the joint Israeli-American military operation that sparked the war with Iran at the end of February.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's tense presidential run-off campaign feels like a psychological thriller</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faa64628fc0054db6ee7d770346625b25a71fb2e6321a4ea6457b82d6eed0f1b</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:45:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller--934b659fa2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller" /><summary type="html">Insults traded on social media and a combative debate have intensified the pressure ahead of a fiercely contested presidential run-off on Sunday, with only a few points separating leftist pro-union President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>United-States : Backlash over controversial Ohio midterms campaign ad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b845922df0f5bd41d6c508c8bb370caaf188dd00cb54210c5cf516e141ba97b7</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:04:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/united-states-backlash-over-controversial-ohio-midterms-campaign-ad--5240dc639fc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/united-states-backlash-over-controversial-ohio-midterms-campaign-ad" /><summary type="html">The backlash over an Ohio campaign advertisement attacking Amy Acton, the Democratic nominee for governor, spread beyond the state's borders Thursday, causing fresh headaches for Republicans with less than two weeks until the midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>🇧🇷 Brazil: Why should you care about the country's elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2747237bb158a462c3f8eea7b0b12b4c9fa72197c7f554fafe9df70beb5895a3</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T06:48:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-brazil-why-should-you-care-about-the-country-s-elections--cb8adc17f6e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-brazil-why-should-you-care-about-the-country-s-elections" /><summary type="html">🗳️ On October 25, a runoff election in #Brazil could change the political landscape of #LatinAmerica. In the first round, #FlavioBolsonaro, son of ex-president Jair #Bolsonaro, beat incumbent President Luiz Inacio #Lula da Silva by a little over two million votes.
 
👉 But why should you care about who will win this second round? Our journalist Vitoria Barreto explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula, Bolsonaro clash on living costs, corruption in final Brazil election debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b3195b867e6a0dd9e2c1f26b5e9c9ddb418b2e89e9f7002b4d39bce0b25765c</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T02:20:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-lula-bolsonaro-strike-calmer-tone-in-final-brazil-election-debate--b19d1562960b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-lula-bolsonaro-strike-calmer-tone-in-final-brazil-election-debate" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and sight-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro faced off Friday in their second and final debate ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff election. The two candidates repeated their campaign proposals, focusing on the cost of living and security, while exchanging ⁠allegations of corruption.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>New York City votes to ban Central Park horse-drawn carriages after decades of debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf69494a46960a7cdf3b74e91495a2013c3ccaeaac96905288d83e607a30fd65</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T00:18:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-new-york-city-votes-to-ban-central-park-horse-drawn-carriages-after-decades-of-debate--1d892a705666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-new-york-city-votes-to-ban-central-park-horse-drawn-carriages-after-decades-of-debate" /><summary type="html">New York's city council voted Thursday in favor of a measure to ban horse-drawn carriages in Central Park, a tourist attraction that has been controversial for years. Mayor Zohran Mamdani is expected to sign the ban into law which would go into effect starting in June 2028</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Emirati diplomat could become next UN chief despite human rights concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73e53d306da421f5cef3d86517cd5c9444f94549aab4cbdefa92a4fcc05ae636</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T21:18:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-emirati-diplomat-could-become-next-un-chief-despite-human-rights-concerns-uae-sudan-un-secr--36fc529e3344.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-emirati-diplomat-could-become-next-un-chief-despite-human-rights-concerns-uae-sudan-un-secretary-general-lana-nusseibeh" /><summary type="html">Human rights defenders are sounding the alarm over the United Arab Emirates’ nomination of its former envoy Lana Nusseibeh to be the next UN Secretary General. They say electing a diplomat from the UAE, a country with a questionable human rights record that is accused of backing forces behind a massacre in Sudan, could spell “catastrophe” for the UN.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Vance tells Republicans to 'stop whining' after Ramaswamy attack ad in Ohio governor's race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8531a460090e1992bfb353aeeeffdbadc1129e29026f217a81208cdf467b60cf</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:05:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/vance-tells-republicans-to-stop-whining-after-ramaswamy-attack-ad-in-ohio-governor-s-race--58bc4a1ae869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/vance-tells-republicans-to-stop-whining-after-ramaswamy-attack-ad-in-ohio-governor-s-race" /><summary type="html">US Vice President JD Vance on Wednesday defended an explosive attack ad by Republican Vivek Ramaswamy’s campaign against his Democratic rival in the Ohio governor’s race, telling fellow Republicans to "stop whining" about it and go win the race. The ad features ​Democrat Amy Acton’s ‌estranged mother, Donna Arthur, disputing Acton’s account of a childhood she says involved a period of homelessness and sexual abuse. ⁠Arthur, whom Acton says she has not seen since 1978, urges Ohioans not to vote for her daughter. Acton has said she was sexually abused by her stepfather when she was 12. Her mother stayed with the ‌stepfather, who was charged with rape but fled the state and was never tried. He died in 2004. Acton said she ⁠and her brother were removed from her mother's custody for severe abuse, neglect and sexual abuse. Acton's brother has supported her account. FRANCE 24's Catherine Viette reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Back to the Bolsonaros? Brazil's presidential run-off goes down to the wire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:683289d116f5f48e06e7ec198d35273a4d005cf50ba10c44f336edf12744dc8e</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T18:18:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-back-to-the-bolsonaros-brazil-presidential-run-off-goes-down-to-the-wire--976659f1cff7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-back-to-the-bolsonaros-brazil-presidential-run-off-goes-down-to-the-wire" /><summary type="html">Brazil's future is within the margin of error ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff: most of the latest polls put the far-right's Flavio Bolsonaro ahead of left-wing incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva – a lead that's narrowed after last weekend's acrimonious debate.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ahead of US and Israeli elections, 3-day joint attack on Iran 'would not radically change conflict'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70bcf6dec287c1bb7201f3c1610c3609474fbc9d3c6d85bb4f241965f7b0d195</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:36:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict--cb0fe2d52092.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Federico Donelli, Associate Professor of International Relations in the Department of Political and Social Sciences at the University of Trieste in Italy. Can another three days of military strikes achieve what eight months of confrontation have failed to deliver? Donelli challenges the assumption that a short, intensive offensive would necessarily produce a decisive political outcome. He argues, "the real question is whether military pressure is intended to constrain Iran's capacity, or to pressure Iran to sit on the table." And whether they can translate that capacity into a sustainable political outcome without provoking a wider regional crisis. Regardless, Donelli reminds us that "Iran still has leverage over the US."</summary></entry><entry><title>Georgia on Democrats’ minds: Powering up the Black vote to counter Trump's meddling</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f6a5551fb2f421b1e00f6821f8ca448099f3987c134893d1bdf6b11b92f12e7</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:43:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-georgia-on-democrats-minds-powering-up-black-vote-counter-trump-meddling--7648a88f5f00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-georgia-on-democrats-minds-powering-up-black-vote-counter-trump-meddling" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's push to redistrict congressional maps and a Georgia state election law disproportionately affecting African Americans are aimed at diluting the power of the Black vote. Six decades after Atlanta was at the heart of the civil rights movement that granted Blacks in the southern states the right to vote, the community is fighting back.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's sprawling favelas require long-term urban planning solutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:085b8d5d9d75128d9b0af68726a44f772f7f058f05e1b4688ce65a0bc597e3f3</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:31:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261022-brazil-s-sprawling-favelas-require-long-term-urban-planning-solutions--4857e607d4ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261022-brazil-s-sprawling-favelas-require-long-term-urban-planning-solutions" /><summary type="html">As Brazilians head to the polls on Sunday for the second round of presidential elections, our correspondents take us to the heart of the country's favelas, where residents live in unsanitary conditions. Over the past 40 years, the area occupied by Brazilian favelas has almost tripled in size. They now cover around 460,000 hectares, compared with 53,700 in 1985.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Trump admin 'destroying' US democracy with 'autocratic, terrorist version of Christian nationalism'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61228d6eb49f39adbcb6c88cbf439ca98c65e0b269b574d5d7dd2fed399068a6</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:11:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261021-trump-admin-destroying-us-democracy-with-autocratic-terrorist-version-of-christian-national--f98b028aa6cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261021-trump-admin-destroying-us-democracy-with-autocratic-terrorist-version-of-christian-nationalism" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes former US Assistant Secretary of Defense Jim Townsend and former US Air Force officer Michael (Mikey) Weinstein, founder and president of the Military Religious Freedom Foundation. Is American military power becoming an instrument of political and religious coercion, both at home and abroad? From the reported restrictions on Ukraine's access to Starlink satellite communications to the Trump administration's overtures towards Russian President Vladimir Putin and the growing controversy over religious ideology within the Pentagon, the two guests offer a stark assessment of the direction of American foreign and defence policy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump exploits France riots to push false immigration claims ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3487def1fa0a4d2f2fe14b10e1da6090e7c07ef4fea96c0e0c04aaa6e1c1349b</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms--d75f9c282915.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump and his inner circle are using unrest in France to push unsubstantiated claims blaming the riots on immigration, even showing French protest footage at midterm rallies. But there is no evidence linking immigration to the unrest, and it's prompted French President Emmanuel Macron to accuse world leaders of making "stupid comments" at France's expense. Trump's focus comes as Republicans face mounting pressure ahead of the midterms and his approval rating hits a reported record low.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Some Brazilians long associated with the left now shift towards Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:780c02777b1dfb80af79772c64cf5b20a4e8af14a868f1ee1776aeafff5fe72c</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro--276f6e2ecc23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">In the first round of Brazil’s presidential elections, Flavio Bolsonaro got the most votes in 15 electoral districts in the North Zone of Rio de Janeiro, compared with 9 for Lula. This part of the city, long associated with the left and the social policies of Lula’s Workers’ Party, is now shifting towards former president Jair Bolsonaro’s son.</summary></entry><entry><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84fb116eb352c83f61e06317b6c28cb55e5c7968cb16db76daf952a89d87e368</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:44:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin---0e5c90a4d0ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.</summary></entry><entry><title>Concerns mount over artificial intelligence as Silicon Valley sees AI boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e750603ff62a687d16e073b2c75b8d3a16925c727c1c74d709141c69d6204b18</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261021-concerns-mount-over-artificial-intelligence-as-silicon-valley-sees-ai-boom--fb07f401c7af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261021-concerns-mount-over-artificial-intelligence-as-silicon-valley-sees-ai-boom" /><summary type="html">Tuesday, October 20 saw protests in more than 50 US cities against the rise of artificial intelligence. Demonstrators are calling for a moratorium on AI development, and the sentiment is shared by many: according to a recent study, 71 percent of Americans believe AI will lead to job losses. In the heart of Silicon Valley, record investment is now on a collision course with public fear and uncertainty. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent and Valérie Defert report, with Wassim Cornet.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Trump campaigns in deep-red states, fearing Democratic wave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:840d8c538fe97ec0ef7d99bc3df60b44b0c18fa8ffae585c29901dfebd6f3651</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigns-in-deep-red-states-fearing-democratic-wave--f35171296156.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigns-in-deep-red-states-fearing-democratic-wave" /><summary type="html">The midterm elections are just two weeks away in the United States and Donald Trump is stumping for candidates in states that he won by double digits in 2024. Polls showing support for the Republican Party is slipping drastically, even in some deep red states. Story by Monte Francis.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI on the ballot? Voters in US midterms revolt against data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6c7dbca9de2b903426a839b31226f4e65605c7bccdc2a36a8054a7290c8c884</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T22:45:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261020-ai-on-the-ballot-voters-in-us-midterms-revolt-against-data-centres--00ec068c2493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261020-ai-on-the-ballot-voters-in-us-midterms-revolt-against-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Two weeks out from the US midterm elections, there's bipartisan pushback against data centres that suck the water and power out of communities. Just two years ago, ChatGPT was still a brand-new thing, and AI was admired with awe by most voters. Like in 2024, the hot-button issue in swing constituencies remains inflation, or "the price of eggs". But anxiety over the end of the month is now coupled with anxiety over the end of the world.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil’s presidential candidates push to have one another disqualified ahead of run-off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35e033b594643cb9629e15aa9f54a97d81069a4dd77dd4fb7b8fbeaa8c5a25f4</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T20:59:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261020-lula-campaign-seeks-disqualify-bolsonoro-from-brazil-presidential-vote-over-meta-interferen--28674a91421b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261020-lula-campaign-seeks-disqualify-bolsonoro-from-brazil-presidential-vote-over-meta-interference" /><summary type="html">Both candidates in Brazil's presidential election called for their rival's disqualification Tuesday over allegations of social media malfeasance, according to court filings. Left-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s campaign said they will request the annulment of right-wing rival Flavio Bolsonaro's candidacy over alleged election interference by tech giant Meta, while Bolsonaro's team is accusing Lula of "abuse of power" in the mass sharing of government postings on WhatsApp.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump campaigning in Republican strongholds amid slide in polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:639dc70bd3bb36f3239a12182e0d47619f9fd28b8d8b9f5d98a6943bc12f3b0f</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T20:13:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigning-in-republican-strongholds-amid-slide-in-polls--38598da6800a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigning-in-republican-strongholds-amid-slide-in-polls" /><summary type="html">With the midterm elections fast approaching, US President Donald Trump is stumping for candidates in states that he won by double digits in 2024. Despite what he says, it’s a sign of what Trump and the Republican party are fearing: with polls showing GOP support slip drastically even in some deep red states. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Trump approval rating falls to new low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:808264121104f1322c8856c599a6e155a1dd2690c7f57513e0e3200632c948e1</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:22:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-us-midterm-elections-trump-approval-rating-falls-to-new-low--bc210483afa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-us-midterm-elections-trump-approval-rating-falls-to-new-low" /><summary type="html">With US President Donald Trump’s approval rating falling to a record low of 31%, Republicans are facing mounting concerns ahead of November’s midterm elections. Republicans are at risk of losing control of the House of Representatives, but how big could the Democrats’ gains be? FRANCE 24’s International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Alberta votes to remain part of Canada in victory for PM Carney</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8c24bed2784b83638e045194cca86113123c78dbed98c09533bb92d1aaff988</id><updated>2026-10-25T13:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:45:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-alberta-votes-to-remain-part-of-canada-in-victory-for-pm-carney--80a5f9f09a54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-alberta-votes-to-remain-part-of-canada-in-victory-for-pm-carney" /><summary type="html">Voters in oil-rich Alberta overwhelmingly backed remaining in Canada in the province's first-ever referendum on separation, with early results on Tuesday delivering a boost to Prime Minister Mark Carney’s push for national unity amid US President Donald Trump’s trade war and annexation threats.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
